Proton's set_focus() grabs and ungrabs the pointer (wait_grab_pointer),
which generates crossing events; cwm, OpenBSD's default window manager,
activates a client on every EnterNotify regardless of its mode and sends
WM_TAKE_FOCUS again: an endless loop (explorer.exe, the program and
wineserver busy with an idle notepad).  Ignore WM_TAKE_FOCUS when the
window already is the foreground window and has the X input focus.

